Well, I've been playing NH on a DOS box for a long time, so maybe I'm
biased in looking at MacNH. But:

Color is _very_ important to me when playing. While I can play without
it, it helps a lot. I have a hard time distinguishing between the
washed-out colors in the default Defaults file. I haven't played with
the palette option in there yet- that could also use some more
documentation (I'm assuming that it's a series of color id's, each a
sequence of three hex digits specifying RGB, separated by /'s.).
Maybe playing with this will give me richer colors. We'll see.

The only other complaint I have, really, is suport for number_pad.
The functionality here (on my enhanced keyboard) seems to be somewhat
reversed- with OPTIONS=!number_pad, i can use the number pad to move
around, but with OPTIONS=number_pad, I can't! Furthermore, neither
setting does the handy-dandy mapping of the letter-movement keys to
jump, kick, etc (which I greatly prefer).

Other than that, now that I have a reasonable version of NH on my
mac, I can retire my DOS box :)

Thanks, Dev team!

